                                "sense_id": "9da3bfba-b695-3712-bb59-4d5f3dca0ec0",
                                "text": "Three green bonnets at church one day / Dulcie and Daisy and Dorothy May / Three green bonnets that nod in a row/ Each bonnet tied with a green ribbon bow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23b977e6-209b-41ee-ad0e-32a2b8a6b03d",
                                "sense_id": "9da3bfba-b695-3712-bb59-4d5f3dca0ec0",
                                "text": "\"Probably most people hate the name they've got,\" she said. \"Take Dulcie.\"\n\"It's not bad,\" he said slowly. \"It's sort of exotic.\"\nThat was a word he had decided to adopt.\n\"No, it isn't. It's awful, really. It means 'sweet'. And Dulcie's a plump girl with fair hair and blue eyes. A complexion.\""
                            }
